132 0 obj
<</Type/Annot/Subtype/Widget/AP<</N 852 0 R>>/DA(0 g /Helv 6.4 Tf)/DR<</Encoding<</PDFDocEncoding 21 0 R>>/Font<</Helv 20 0 R>>>>/F 4/FT/Tx/Ff 4096/P 218 0 R/Rect[93.6 319.92 799.56 388.56]/T(Proposed Situation_2)/TU(Proposed Situation)/Q 0/BS<</S/S/W 1>>/V(\(1\) THIS LOT: keep lot 00004515 in quarantine. QA to decide between \(a\) release under a deviation, possible only if an endotoxin result showing < 1 EU/ml is obtained \(vendor actual value/raw data with adequate sensitivity, or QC/contract-lab LAL test of the retained sample\), or \(b\) full requalification. Lot is not to be used until QA approves disposition. \(2\) PERMANENT: revise RMS-3333 so the < 1 EU/ml limit is verified by in-house/contract endotoxin testing per lot \(COA endotoxin = report only\), unless a QA-approved risk assessment justifies a different limit. Correct the ambiguous endotoxin wording, the 'Antiform' typo and the expiry rule \(must not exceed manufacturer expiry\). Add vendor product no. 599-12X. Update the CompCello supplier file and quality agreement, and set up a central vendor change-notification inbox.)>>
endobj

133 0 obj
<</Type/Annot/Subtype/Widget/AP<</N 854 0 R>>/DA(0 g /Helv 6.4 Tf)/DR<</Encoding<</PDFDocEncoding 21 0 R>>/Font<</Helv 20 0 R>>>>/F 4/FT/Tx/Ff 4096/P 218 0 R/Rect[93.6 234.35999 799.56 303.12]/T(Change Justification_2)/TU(Change Justification)/Q 0/BS<</S/S/W 1>>/V(Endotoxin is a critical attribute for plasmid DNA manufacture, and RMS-3333 relies on the supplier COA for the < 1 EU/ml release criterion. The supplier changed this to report-only and the notification was not received by a functional owner, so the change was never assessed. If the RMS and the control strategy are not aligned, every future CompCello lot will fail COA review the same way, or material could be released without evidence of endotoxin compliance. Formal change control is needed to assess the vendor change, decide disposition of the current lot, and update the specification, supplier qualification records and vendor-communication process. This protects product quality and the client run schedule.)>>
endobj

134 0 obj
<</Type/Annot/Subtype/Widget/AP<</N 850 0 R>>/DA(0 g /Helv 6.4 Tf)/DR<</Encoding<</PDFDocEncoding 21 0 R>>/Font<</Helv 20 0 R>>>>/F 4/FT/Tx/Ff 4096/P 218 0 R/Rect[93.6 405.36 799.56 474]/T(Current Situation_2)/TU(Current Situation)/Q 0/BS<</S/S/W 1>>/V(RMS-3333 \(issued 12 Apr 2024, approved QA 17 May 2024\) lists 'Endotoxin Level \(post-irradiation - only report the results\)' with specification < 1 EU/ml. The CompCello COA for lot 00004515 \(mfd 01 May 2025, QA release 29 May 2025, expiry 01 May 2027\) shows endotoxin specification 'EU/ml - Report Result' and result '< 5 EU/ml'. Every other COA test matches RMS-3333 and conforms \(Appearance White/Liquid, Irradiation Cert. Conforms, Defoaming 3 s, Irradiation 28 / 33 kGy\). The supplier no longer certifies endotoxin against a limit, and the reported value does not demonstrate < 1 EU/ml. QA has rejected COA-based release; the lot is on hold and the GMP plasmid run is at risk. The RMS endotoxin row also contradicts itself \(title says 'report only', spec column says < 1 EU/ml\).)>>
endobj

